[00:09.90] Out in the West Texas town of El Paso
[00:13.34] I fell in love with a Mexican girl
[00:17.76] Nighttime would find me in Rosa's cantina
[00:22.66] Music would play and Felina would whirl
[00:28.10] Blacker than night were the eyes of Felina
[00:32.20] Wicked and evil while casting a spell
[00:37.52] My love was deep for this Mexican maiden
[00:41.38] I was in love but in vain, I could tell
[00:46.14] One night a wild young cowboy came in
[00:51.04] Wild as the West Texas wind
[00:58.90] Dashing and daring, a drink he was sharing
[01:02.86] With wicked Felina, the girl that I loved
[01:06.74] So in anger I challenged his right for the love of this maiden
[01:11.94] Down went his hand for the gun that he wore
[01:16.54] My challenge was answered in less than a heartbeat
[01:21.60] The handsome young stranger lay dead on the floor
[01:27.50] Out through the back door of Rosa's I ran
[01:31.06] Out where the horses were tied
[01:39.72] I caught a good one, it looked like it could run
[01:42.86] Up on its back and away I did ride
[01:46.64] Just as fast as I could
[01:49.26] From the West Texas town of El Paso
[01:52.22] Out to the badlands of New Mexico
[01:56.36] Back in El Paso my life would be worthless
[02:01.50] Everything's gone in life, nothing is left
[02:06.18] It's been so long since I've seen the young maiden
[02:10.86] My love is stronger than my fear of death
[02:14.90] I saddled up and away I did go
[02:19.96] Riding alone in the dark
[02:27.80] Maybe tomorrow a bullet may find me
[02:31.70] Tonight nothing's worse than this pain in my heart
[02:35.46] And at last, here I am on the hill, overlooking El Paso
[02:41.30] I can see Rosa's cantina below
[02:45.38] My love is strong and it pushes me onward
[02:50.44] Down off the hill to Felina I go
[02:54.86] Off to my right I see five mounted cowboys
[02:59.66] Off to my left ride a dozen or more
[03:04.98] Shouting and shooting, I can't let them catch me
[03:08.88] I have to make it to Rosa's back door
[03:12.54] Something is dreadfully wrong, for I feel
[03:18.00] A deep burning pain in my side
[03:26.46] Though I am trying to stay in the saddle
[03:29.92] I'm getting weary, unable to ride
[03:33.56] But my love for Felina is strong and I rise where I've fallen
[03:38.96] Though I am weary, I can't stop to rest
[03:43.58] I see the white puff of smoke from the rifle
[03:48.36] I feel the bullet go deep in my chest
[03:54.02] From out of nowhere Felina has found me
[03:57.66] Kissing my cheek as she kneels by my side
[04:03.36] Cradled by two loving arms that I'll die for
[04:06.86] One little kiss and Felina, goodbye
